      "content": "Thanks for that. It seems like you're leaning heavily on the brand names of their previous companies and schools to gauge their \"presence.\" \n\nI'm curious about the others, though. Malik and Tasha clearly have deep technical expertise, and Malik's fintech experience is actually quite high-stakes. Why do you think they wouldn't have that same \"seamless\" feel? Are you suggesting that coming from an HBCU or a different industry might make them appear less authoritative or more \"awkward\" when trying to communicate with our current executive team?",
